      "title": "READ ME",
      "properties": {
        "ue_properties": {
          "widget_ue_connectable": {},
          "version": "7.8",
          "input_ue_unconnectable": {}
        }
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "# [READ ME] RefMod Video Pack (MiniMax H3)\n\n## What this does\nSaves the **motion** of a short clip (a dance, a gesture, a camera move) as a **RefMod** you can load in the **MM RefMod T2V** workflow next to your character.\n\nThe clip's **look** comes along too: the person, clothing and background in it can leak into your video. Clips with a plain background work best.\n\n## Picking the clip\n1. **One clip only.** Keep it short (2 to 4 seconds) and trimmed to the exact movement you want.\n2. Up to **49 frames** are taken, spread evenly across the whole clip (`max_frames`). A long clip gets thinned out and the motion turns choppy.\n3. Fast motion (quick hand moves, fight flurries) gets smoothed into something slower. Slower, clear movements copy best.\n\n## How to use\n1. Put the clip in its own folder inside `ComfyUI/input` (default `input/refmod_video`).\n2. **VIDEO CLIP FOLDER:** type that folder name.\n3. **CREATE REFMOD:** type a name in `name` (for example `hip_sway`). Leave the other settings alone.\n4. **SAVE REFMOD:** `subfolder` = `video` saves it to `models/refmods/video/<name>`.\n5. **Queue.**\n6. In the T2V workflow: click **Refresh RefMods**, then **+ Add RefMod** on the CHARACTER REFMOD node and pick it. **Describe the motion in your prompt too.** The RefMod helps, but the prompt anchors it.\n\n## Links\n- **YouTube:** [youtube.com/@lora-tech](https://www.youtube.com/@lora-tech)\n- **Discord (community, support, 1 on 1 coaching):** [discord.gg/2bqQXKxsxg](https://discord.gg/2bqQXKxsxg)\n- **Patreon:** [patreon.com/LoRAtech](https://www.patreon.com/LoRAtech)\n"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "# [READ ME] RefMod Video Pack (MiniMax H3)\n\n## What this does\nSaves the **motion** of a short clip (a dance, a gesture, a camera move) as a **RefMod** you can load in the **MM RefMod T2V** workflow next to your character.\n\nThe clip's **look** comes along too: the person, clothing and background in it can leak into your video. Clips with a plain background work best.\n\n## Picking the clip\n1. **One clip only.** Keep it short (2 to 4 seconds) and trimmed to the exact movement you want.\n2. Up to **49 frames** are taken, spread evenly across the whole clip (`max_frames`). A long clip gets thinned out and the motion turns choppy.\n3. Fast motion (quick hand moves, fight flurries) gets smoothed into something slower. Slower, clear movements copy best.\n\n## How to use\n1. Put the clip in its own folder inside `ComfyUI/input` (default `input/refmod_video`).\n2. **VIDEO CLIP FOLDER:** type that folder name.\n3. **CREATE REFMOD:** type a name in `name` (for example `hip_sway`). Leave the other settings alone.\n4. **SAVE REFMOD:** `subfolder` = `video` saves it to `models/refmods/video/<name>`.\n5. **Queue.**\n6. In the T2V workflow: click **Refresh RefMods**, then **+ Add RefMod** on the CHARACTER REFMOD node and pick it. **Describe the motion in your prompt too.** The RefMod helps, but the prompt anchors it.\n\n## Links\n- **YouTube:** [youtube.com/@lora-tech](https://www.youtube.com/@lora-tech)\n- **Discord (community, support, 1 on 1 coaching):** [discord.gg/2bqQXKxsxg](https://discord.gg/2bqQXKxsxg)\n- **Patreon:** [patreon.com/LoRAtech](https://www.patreon.com/LoRAtech)\n"
      },
